      "response": "Agency/Agencies loaded: agency-steward, code-reviewer, python-application-engineer, software-test-engineer\nAgency/Agencies delegated: none\nSkills loaded: none\nActual Model selected: observed execution receipt: alias-hermes-chat -> alias-hermes-chat (host)\nRecruited via: inference\n\nCorrectness defects:\n- Uses floor division (`//`), so fractional means are truncated/floored instead of returned. Example: `[1.0, 2.0]` returns `1.0`, not `1.5`.\n- For negative fractional means, `//` floors downward, which is even more surprising. Example: `[-1, -2]` returns `-2`, not `-1.5`.\n- Empty input raises `ZeroDivisionError`; the requested contract is `ValueError`.\n\nCorrected function:\n\n```python\ndef average(values):\n    if not values:\n        raise ValueError(\"average requires at least one value\")\n    return sum(values) / len(values)\n```\n\nFocused regression tests:\n\n```python\nimport pytest\n\n\ndef test_average_returns_fractional_mean_for_floats():\n    assert average([1.0, 2.0]) == 1.5\n\n\ndef test_average_handles_negative_numbers():\n    assert average([-1, -2]) == -1.5\n\n\ndef test_average_rejects_empty_input():\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        average([])\n```\n\nNo files were read or modified, and these tests were not executed.",
